-- title:
--   Weight-2m q-expansions of mod-p modular functions lie in `modPMod`
-- statement:
--   Let $p \ge 5$ be a prime, let $N \ge 1$ be an integer with $p \nmid N$, let $K$ be a field of characteristic $p$, and let $m$ be a natural number. Write $\bar j =$ `jqModC K` $= q^{-1}\cdot$(the reduction to $K$ of the integral power series `jNum`) in $K((q))$, and $\bar j_N =$ `jqNModC K N`, its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$; let $G$ be an element of the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldC K N` $= K(\bar j, \bar j_N) \subseteq K((q))$. Assume `IsModPFormFn K m G`, i.e. both integrality conditions: $G^6\,\bar j^{4m}(\bar j - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar j$, and $G^2\,\bar j^{m}(\bar j - 1728)^{m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar j^{-1}$. Then there exists a power series $\varphi \in K[[q]]$ lying in the submodule [`ModPForms.modPMod N (2m) K`](def/CuspForm_ModPForms.html#L12) — the $K$-span of those power series $\sum_n \overline{a_n} q^n$ arising from a modular form $f$ of weight $2m$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose $q$-expansion coefficients `qCoeff f n` all equal integers $a_n$, reduced into $K$ — whose image in $K((q))$ equals `qexpOfWeight K m G` $= G \cdot (\theta\bar j)^m$, where $\theta \bar j =$ `thetaJ K` $=$ `thetaL K` applied to $\bar j$.
--
--   This is the bridge from holomorphic mod-$p$ modular functions on the modular function field of level $N$ to the $q$-expansion span of weight-$2m$ mod-$p$ modular forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$, in the form used throughout the `ModPForms` development (its content is Katz's base-change and $q$-expansion principle for mod-$p$ modular forms). It removes the hypothesis that $K$ be algebraically closed, and covers weight $0$; it is cited by the cusp-form analogue and by further membership lemmas for `modPMod`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModPForms_exists_mem_modPMod_ofPowerSeries_eq_qexpOfWeight_of_isModPFormFn.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_ModPForms
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ModPFormFn

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
